- Therefore, the new work section (technical content) is approximately 350 words.

The percentage of technical content that remains after removing the "citation_focus_text" is calculated as:
\[
\text{Technical Percentage} = \left( \frac{\text{Length of new work section}}{\text{Total length of introduction}} \right) \times 100 = \left( \frac{350}{500} \right) \times 100 = 70\%
\]

This 70% represents the proportion of the introduction that is directly technical and original, excluding the prior work context. In academic writing, this is a reasonable estimate for the technical content in a well-structured introduction where the new work section dominates the technical contribution.

**Final Answer**: 70%
